WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.634
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Kenan Thompson.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:04.834
This is really cool,
speaking about

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.734
how long you've been
on the show.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:09.734
Aubrey Plaza hosting this week,
the fantastic Aubrey Plaza,

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.934
was, in 2004,
when we were both there,

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:12.968
an intern in the set department.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.133
-Is that not crazy?

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.534
-What a trip.
Now the interns are coming back.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:17.534
That's how long
you've been there.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:18.734
-Yeah, I know.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.467
So I'm going to start hurting
at some point.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.734
-Yeah. I will say --
and I think this reflects

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.367
very well on you --
this is a real reminder --

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.734
be nice to the interns,

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.467
which I'm sure
you always have been.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.567
-1,000%.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:30.901
Like, all this week,
I've been like,

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:34.901
"I feel like I was nice to her,
but do I know for sure?"

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:38.300
-We all do have bad days,
but it's a real mistake

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.400
to take it out on the interns,
because just based on, you know,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.968
life expectancy,
they're going to be around

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.701
after we're long gone.

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:47.868
We were talking about --
You know,

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:49.200
I have authors
on the show a lot.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.501
-Yes, you do.

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:54.033
-And you were lamenting the fact
that you've never been on

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.434
to talk about your book,
because I, of course,

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.701
did not know --
or certainly assumed that

00:00:58.701 --> 00:00:59.734
you hadn't written a book,
but you actually have been

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.267
writing books.

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:06.667
-Yes, I've been dabbling in the
world of authoring, if you will.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.834
And, yeah, I'm very excited to

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.567
present some of my work
here tonight.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.801
-And you write under a pen name.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.133
-I do. A full pen name.
-Okay.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.701
Would you like to leave
and have me introduce you

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:18.834
as your pen name?

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.200
-Oh, that's fun.
Yeah, can we do that?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.200
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.434
-Okay, go ahead.
-Okay, I'm going.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.367
Okay, I'll be right back.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:31.934
-This is really exciting,
everybody.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:36.267
Our next guest is
a science-fiction writer

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.634
with the third
in his "Quark" series.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:43.234
Please welcome the author of
"Quinsley's Nebula,"

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.000
Pernice LaFonk.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.567
Oh, my God.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.100
Mr. LaFonk, what an honor
to have you here.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.501
-Sethly, it is
an honor and a privilege

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:19.133
to be graced with your presence,
as well, my friend.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:22.601
-Now, you are
a science-fiction writer.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.601
Where do you get
your wonderful ideas about

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.701
space and these
fantastic characters?

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:29.300
-Oh, the cosmos provides.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.334
The cosmos
most definitely provides.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.100
And I would just love to
read a bit of my...

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.434
-Do you want to read a passage?
-...my work.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.300
-Well, here we go.
This is so exciting.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.801
And I've read all the books
in the "Quark" series,

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:39.968
so this is very exciting.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:43.767
-And you respect mine.
Thank you very much.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.467
Wonderful.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.234
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:53.367
The name of the book is
"Quinsley's Nebula."

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:57.000
Here is a passage from
Chapter 13, "Beta 4."

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.167
-Your chapters always have
the most wonderful titles.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:04.100
-Yes. Big fan of "Star Wars."

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.801
"There is thunder
on the planet Persephone 9."

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:11.734
Mm.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:14.834
"But it makes not the cracking
sound it does on Earth.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:18.234
Rather,
it makes a different noise

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:22.067
every...single...time.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:26.434
No sound of thunder ever repeats
on this barren planet,

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:29.033
a fact that
Captain Grax Pendlesmith

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:33.400
was unaware of as he steered
his ship to an uneasy landing

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.367
amidst the swirling storm.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.567
'Kerflank!'

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:41.834
went the thunder as
his trusty ship, the Pegaseuss,

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.267
lurched to the right.

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:47.434
'Ba-klamp!' went the next,

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:49.901
followed by a
'Paloma,' 'Shalamar,'

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.167
and, finally, 'Futhermucker.'"

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.434
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
Good times.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.434
-So wonderful.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:03:59.701
-Thank you very much.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:03.367
-And, now, you are doing
a book signing at

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.300
Barnes &amp; Noble tonight?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.601
-Not tonight.

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.000
Very early in the morning,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.734
if you wouldn't mind
showing up at 5:00 a.m.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.634
I will be there promptly
at 5:07.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:14.234
-Now, I don't even think
Barnes &amp; Noble

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.400
is open that early.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.434
Are you doing it outside
the Barnes &amp; Noble?

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:20.601
-If it's ideal, on the sidewalk.

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:23.067
-So you're doing
a book signing on the sidewalk

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.167
outside of Barnes &amp; Noble.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:26.868
-Yes. I'm very brave.
Very brave.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:28.300
And I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.767
Also, I will be introducing
my following, follow-up book,

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.133
"Amazon Boobies on the Moon."

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:37.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.200
So look out for that series.
-Where did you get that idea?

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.534
-I think in the shower.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:47.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.334
-Now, what do you smoke?

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.634
Could I just ask
real quick, Pernice,

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:50.701
what do you usually smoke?

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:53.534
-I think you know.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.801
I think you know.

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.133
We don't want to --
-And this is very exciting.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:01.434
I know that Netflix
is adapting this into a series,

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:05.467
and there is some really
exciting casting news you have.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:06.701
-Is that happening?

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.200
Oh.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.701
I wasn't aware of that.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:14.200
I'm very excited
to hear their plans.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.701
-Do you even
have a Netflix account?

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:21.367
-And could you explain,
what is this Netflix, exactly?

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:22.767
This is fun.

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:25.934
-Pernice LaFonk, you, of course,
are also Kenan Thompson.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.300
You are a dear friend.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.334
Give it up one more time...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.000
for Kenan, everybody.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.167
"SNL" returns and this week with

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.834
host Aubrey Plaza
and musical guest Sam Smith.

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:41.133
We'll be right back with
Jinkx Monsoon.

